Write a Program to implement various types of visualization in python. 


ALGORITHM:
Start the program.
Import Pandas and Matplotlib libraries.
Create sample data using a dictionary.
Convert the data into a Pandas DataFrame.
Display the dataset.
Create a Line Graph for Sales and Profit.
Create a Bar Graph for Expenses.
Create a Histogram for Sales distribution.
Create a Pie Chart for Profit distribution.
Create a Scatter Plot for Sales vs Profit.
Display all graphs using plt.show().
Stop the program.

CODE:
# Program to implement various types of visualization in Python

# Importing libraries
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Creating sample data
data = {
    "Month": ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar", "Apr", "May"],
    "Sales": [200, 250, 300, 280, 350],
    "Profit": [40, 50, 70, 60, 80],
    "Expenses": [160, 200, 230, 220, 270]
}

# Creating DataFrame
df = pd.DataFrame(data)

# Displaying DataFrame
print("COMPANY DATA")
print(df)

# ---------------- LINE GRAPH ----------------
plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))

plt.plot(df["Month"], df["Sales"], marker='o', label="Sales")
plt.plot(df["Month"], df["Profit"], marker='s', label="Profit")

plt.title("Line Graph")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Amount")
plt.legend()
plt.grid(True)

plt.show()

# ---------------- BAR GRAPH ----------------
plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))

plt.bar(df["Month"], df["Expenses"])

plt.title("Bar Graph")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Expenses")

plt.show()

# ---------------- HISTOGRAM ----------------
plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))

plt.hist(df["Sales"], bins=5)

plt.title("Histogram")
plt.xlabel("Sales")
plt.ylabel("Frequency")

plt.show()

# ---------------- PIE CHART ----------------
plt.figure(figsize=(6,6))

plt.pie(df["Profit"], labels=df["Month"], autopct='%1.1f%%')

plt.title("Pie Chart of Profit")

plt.show()

# ---------------- SCATTER PLOT ----------------
plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))

plt.scatter(df["Sales"], df["Profit"])

plt.title("Scatter Plot")
plt.xlabel("Sales")
plt.ylabel("Profit")

plt.show()

